  "proved_bridges": {
    "parallel_geometry": "For even period n, color=(link direction, sum of vertex coordinates mod 2) gives eight disjoint independent-link blocks. A uniform color choice covers every link with probability1/8.",
    "actual_product_law": "The actual fixed-exterior original 4D Wilson Gibbs law for an independent block equals the product of actual normalized one-link laws, as probability measures on the auxiliary link variables. Unselected auxiliary coordinates retain Haar law and are ignored by blockUpdate.",
    "actual_influence": "The compact covariance bound is range(F)*range(G)/4. Integration of the actual source derivative proves |nu_B(G)-nu_A(G)|<=beta range(G)||B-A|| and <=2 beta range(G) if only one unit staple changes. The actual exterior action cancels using the proved Wilson/Haar dictionary.",
    "finite_path_sum": "For a nonnegative finite C with row sums<=alpha<1, the explicitly summed D=I+C+C^2+... satisfies (I-C)D=I, row sums<=1/(1-alpha), and D_ij<=alpha^d(i,j)/(1-alpha) under the stated finite-range/distance hypotheses.",
    "actual_open_chain": "The original full transfer kernel K defines a genuine Fin-k path law. Its boundary message b_k=T^k1 is positive, continuous and gauge invariant. Gluing two k-edge branches gives the exact normalized midpoint density b_k^2/integral b_k^2. The chain retains the original K half-spatial endpoint weights; no alternative endpoint Wilson action or periodic trace formula is asserted.",
    "actual_vacuum_limit": "For A=T/||T||, the actual positive normalized ground psi and c=integral psi>0, ||A^k1-c psi||_2<=q^k||1-c psi||_2. The actual open-chain midpoint expectations converge to pi=psi^2 Haar, with error<=4||F|| exp(24 beta V)q^k, q=1-exp(-24 beta V)."
  },
  "natural_math_review_not_lean_closure": {
    "neighbor_dictionary": "For nondegenerate n>=3, each selected link has18 distinct plaquette neighbors, with each changed neighbor affecting one of six staples. Combined with the proved one-staple estimate this suggests alpha<=36 beta. The full geometry/TV comparison/Gibbs comparison binding is not claimed formalized.",
    "small_beta_range": "The conservative sufficient condition alpha<1 is beta<1/36 in the repo normalization. It is a strong-coupling route and does not extend to the required weak-coupling continuum trajectory.",
    "published_comparison": "Rebeschini and van Handel, Corollary2.6 and2.8, provide Gibbs comparison via a convergent influence series under their full hypotheses. The new matrix theorem alone does not establish those hypotheses or compare Gibbs measures.",
    "published_strong_coupling": "Shen, Zhu and Zhu prove lattice functional inequalities and clustering at small inverse coupling. Their SU(2),d=4 threshold translates from coefficient N beta_paper to repo coefficient beta_repo as beta_repo<1/24. No continuum or physical-transfer conclusion is imported from this theorem.",
    "clock_and_limits": "A constant number of color choices does not equal a bounded amount of physical transfer time. The fixed-cutoff limit k->infinity does not justify exchanging the slab, thermodynamic and ultraviolet limits. Entire color blocks grow with volume, so the existing exp(4 beta |B|) comparison cannot simply be used unchanged.",
    "eight_color_coupling": "For even n>=4 and alpha=36 beta<1, the symmetric18-neighbor influence majorant has row and column sums alpha. A product of maximal one-link conditional couplings for a uniformly selected color gives expected Hamming disagreement <=[1-(1-alpha)/8] times the old disagreement. This natural-math synthesis has volume-independent auxiliary update contraction but a whole-configuration diameter prefactor. The actual TV/maximal-coupling construction is not Lean-certified here, and auxiliary update time is not physical transfer time."
  },
