  "precise_missing_estimate": {
    "physical_poincare": "For actual pi_a=psi_a^2 Haar and actual full ground-transformed P_a, prove Var_pi_a(f)<=C/a E_P_a(f) with C independent of cutoff and volume, for centered gauge-invariant tests and the required completion. With positivity this yields an excited/top bound <=1-a/C for sufficiently small a.",
    "aggregate_block_route": "Prove Var_pi(f)<=C_AT(a) sum_B w_B E_QB(f) and sum_B w_B E_QB(f)<=C_comp(a) E_P(f), with a C_AT(a) C_comp(a) uniformly bounded. The whole original-Wilson color independence does not give the first inequality for pi. Singleton aggregation loses site count, whereas separate whole-color comparisons lose exp(8 beta |B|).",
    "current_rate_diagnostic": "For the illustrative scaling V_a~a^-3, beta_a~b log(1/a), and k_a~tau/a, k_a exp(-24 beta_a V_a)->0. Consequently the proved fixed-cutoff ratio bound supplies no uniform physical-time contraction. This is a conditional scaling diagnostic, not a derived physical trajectory.",
    "independent_review": "A separate agent reviewed the even-period geometry, measure-level factorization, exact law distinctions and physical-clock losses without editing the new proof sources."
  },
  "remaining": [
